                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27eaa3d5-5f8e-3546-8536-0b23a9b2dc72",
                        "entry_id": "b4e52382-c8d7-373f-81cf-6d3e568bb776",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Empereur, dans un contexte romain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6365f5dc-73ba-4b76-8e3b-1f884d34105f",
                                "sense_id": "27eaa3d5-5f8e-3546-8536-0b23a9b2dc72",
                                "text": "Il [Auguste] s'était fait donner tous les titres (…) Imperator et consul, il commandait les armées."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6bb89e4-6dfa-4693-a836-f1b773c8121c",
                                "sense_id": "27eaa3d5-5f8e-3546-8536-0b23a9b2dc72",
                                "text": "Et sur elle courbé, l’ardent Imperator\n Vit dans ses larges yeux étoilés de points d’or\n Toute une mer immense où fuyaient des galères."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "261b6e32-c782-4bda-82fa-284616514277",
                                "sense_id": "27eaa3d5-5f8e-3546-8536-0b23a9b2dc72",
                                "text": "Ces pauvres petits succès d’écolier bien noté étaient, pour son imagination d’adolescent, des triomphes d’imperator romain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60c34462-8064-4301-8a90-eb7b6ab38595",
                                "sense_id": "27eaa3d5-5f8e-3546-8536-0b23a9b2dc72",
                                "text": "Ce doit être un fin régal ce genre d’inspection équestre dans la tourbe des captifs ; ils ont bien raison de ne pas s’en priver. On regarde de haut en bas sans se salir les bottes, en clignant de l’œil sous le cigare avec des mouvements de cravache à l’impérator."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e118a3fa-5b29-4f62-817c-a86245de1b62",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4e52382-c8d7-373f-81cf-6d3e568bb776",
                        "source_sense_id": "27eaa3d5-5f8e-3546-8536-0b23a9b2dc72",
                        "target_lang_word": "imperator",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "imperator",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e902f14c-b4f0-38ce-87d0-48b6f130e24f",
                                        "entry_id": "5c600a9b-cbc9-3075-b316-a08551617e62",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An emperor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24e5075c-74f0-4dee-972e-0b4400e43736",
                                                "sense_id": "e902f14c-b4f0-38ce-87d0-48b6f130e24f",
                                                "text": "But to compensate in some degree for what was then taken away, the custom was introduced of bestowing what was termed Triumphalia Ornamenta, that is, permission to receive the titles bestowed upon, and to appear in public with the robes worn by the imperatores of the commonwealth when they triumphed, and to bequeath to their descendants triumphal statues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11fdbcf3-f783-4a95-8e9c-4e0fa15f56ea",
                                                "sense_id": "e902f14c-b4f0-38ce-87d0-48b6f130e24f",
                                                "text": "Modern emperors and consuls of the year VIII. are no more the imperatores of ancient Rome, and modern religious organizations are but the phantasms of mediæval corporations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e31c3f3-d49d-43cb-95e6-be619bf965ec",
                                                "sense_id": "e902f14c-b4f0-38ce-87d0-48b6f130e24f",
                                                "text": "He said cautiously, \"I do not think it right, Imperator.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885a4924-b82c-43dd-b182-e2b2b2094078",
                                                "sense_id": "e902f14c-b4f0-38ce-87d0-48b6f130e24f",
                                                "text": "Given the sudden proliferation of self-portraits on the coins of all the imperatores of this period, many of whom certainly had not received such a privilege, such an unattested grant to Antony need not be assumed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
